  "summary": "Ruth confronts Iain with Kerry's email. He admits it: his first sleepless week, a web form, then a small lie he couldn't take back once he liked her. Sam tells her to 'be the hedge'. Ruth forgives him on three terms, and the weeks that follow are Oriental Bay, a school concert and good-morning texts after his shifts. Then a text meant for his daughter lands in her thread: he's moving out by 30 May.",
